{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "parts.html.j2" as parts %}
{% block title %}Check every day: {{ product_name() }}{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
<p class="back"><a href="{{ url('manage') }}">Back to Manage</a></p>
<h1 class="page-title">Check every day</h1>
{% if problem %}<p class="error" role="alert">{{ problem }}</p>{% endif %}
{% if not installed %}
<p>No daily check is set up, so servers are only checked when someone asks.</p>
{% elif another_home %}
<p class="error">The daily check on this machine runs another copy of this tool, so this one's servers aren't being checked by it, and it can't be changed from here.</p>
{% elif running is sameas false %}
<p class="error">A daily check is set up{% if time_known %} for {{ at }}{% endif %}, but its timer isn't running, so it won't happen. Save a time to start it{% if not time_known %}: that replaces what was set up by hand{% endif %}.</p>
{% elif running is none %}
<p class="error">A daily check is set up{% if time_known %} for {{ at }}{% endif %}, but this page can't tell whether its timer is running. Whoever looks after this machine can check with <code>checker schedule show</code>.</p>
{% else %}
{% if time_known %}<p>A daily check runs at {{ at }}, this machine's time.</p>{% else %}<p>A timer is set up by hand, at a time this page can't read. Saving a time here replaces it.</p>{% endif %}
{% if on_a_mac %}<p class="note">On a Mac it runs only while someone is logged in at this machine.</p>{% endif %}
{% if lingering is sameas false %}<p class="error">It runs only while someone is logged in to this machine. To run it with nobody logged in, whoever looks after this machine needs to run <code>sudo loginctl enable-linger</code> for the account this web server uses.</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if not another_home %}<p class="note">Each day it checks every server, works out the results, writes a report, and deletes evidence past its retention period, keeping each server's baseline. Keep this machine switched on: if it's off or asleep at that time, the check runs late. A notify command, if one is set on the command line, is told what needs a look. The AI advisor isn't asked.</p>{% endif %}
{% if stops %}
<h2>Servers it can't check</h2>
<p class="note">It leaves these out until they're put right, so they show as out of date on the Servers page.</p>
<ul>{% for name, why in stops %}<li><a href="{{ url('manage_server') }}?host={{ name | urlencode }}"><strong>{{ name }}</strong></a>: {{ why }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% endif %}
{% if not another_home %}<form method="post" action="{{ url('schedule_save') }}">
  {{ csrf_input }}
  <label>Time of day <small>This machine's time.</small> <input type="time" name="at" value="{{ at }}" required></label>
  {{ parts.confirm(with_code=code_needed) }}
  <button>{% if installed %}Save this time{% else %}Check every day at this time{% endif %}</button>
</form>{% endif %}
{% if uses_agent %}<p class="note">A server that logs in with an SSH agent needs its key already unlocked when the check runs, since nobody is there to type a passphrase.</p>{% endif %}
{% if installed and not another_home %}
<h2>Stop it</h2>
<p>Nobody is told if checks stop, so servers could go unchecked unnoticed. If you think a server was broken into, stopping this also stops evidence past its retention period from being deleted each day, but a check started from a page still deletes it: raise the days kept in Settings too.</p>
<form method="post" action="{{ url('schedule_stop') }}">
  {{ csrf_input }}
  {{ parts.confirm(with_code=code_needed) }}
  <button>Stop the daily check</button>
</form>
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
